Third-party components (not complete)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

1) MicroPython

   Prebuilt images named esp32_s3_flipbuddy_*.bin on GitHub Releases embed a
   MicroPython runtime (v1.27 for the 0.1.0 image) and platform pieces from
   the MicroPython ESP32 build. Those stay under their upstream licenses
   (MicroPython is primarily MIT; see https://github.com/micropython/micropython
   and ESP-IDF notices for the build).

   FlipBuddy modules frozen into the image are MIT as in this repository.
   The combined .bin is not "MIT only."

2) MPU6050 / GY-521 (mpu6050.py)

   Portions from Olivier Lenoir (MIT, Copyright (c) 2021-2022).
   DMP-related data and register usage relate to InvenSense / community
   ports (for example i2cdevlib / Jeff Rowberg lineage). See the file header
   and those projects for detail.

3) AP mode / captive portal ideas (ap_mode.py)

   Patterns from https://github.com/metachris/micropython-captiveportal
   (Chris Hager, MIT). See the file header.

4) Host tooling

   Optional PC tools (esptool, mpremote, ampy, ruff, pre-commit, gitleaks,
   and so on) have their own licenses when you install them. They are not
   part of the on-device firmware.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Redistributing frozen images
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

If you redistribute a FlipBuddy Release .bin, keep this NOTICE and the
upstream licenses that apply to MicroPython and any other embedded pieces.
Do not describe the whole binary as original FlipBuddy MIT-only code.
